  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string  SSS  of length NNN.\r\n\n\r\nCount the number of ways of choosing 444 integers L1L_1L1​, R1R_1R1​, L2L_2L2​, R2R_2R2​,  such that :-\n\n\n $1$  $\\leq$  $L_1$  $\\leq$ $R_1$ $\\lt$  $L_2$  $\\leq$ $R_2$  $\\leq $ $N$  \n   $R_1- L_1$  $=$ $R_2-L_2$  \n  string $T$ $=$ $S[L_1...R_1]$ + $S[L_2...R_2]$ is palindrome\n\n\n  $[$ $L_1$, $R_1$, $L_2$, $R_2$ $]$ $=$ $[1,1,3,3]$ \n  $[$ $L_1$, $R_1$, $L_2$, $R_2$ $]$ $=$ $[3,3,4,4]$ \n  $[$ $L_1$, $R_1$, $L_2$, $R_2$ $]$ $=$ $[1,1,4,4]$",
    "constraints": [
      "$1$ $\\leq$ $T$  $\\leq$ $10^5$",
      "$1$ $\\leq$ $|S|$ $\\leq$ $10^5$",
      "$S$  contains only lowercase English letters",
      "the sum of $|S|$ over all test cases does not exceed $500,000$",
      "Example Input",
      "Example Output"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer $T$ denoting the number of test cases. The description of\n        T test cases follows.\n    Each testcase contains a single string $S$.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer, Number of ways to select $4$ integers which satisfy the given property",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": []
  },
